{"chunk_id": "4e03b20f996c", "text": "Garuda continues his quest to seize the Amrita (Soma), overcoming the divine defenses set by the gods. After slaughtering powerful Yakshas and extinguishing a vast ring of celestial fire by drinking up the waters of many rivers, he reaches the guarded nectar. Shrinking his body, he slips through a deadly revolving steel wheel and blinds the two fiery serpents guarding the treasure, tearing them apart. Garuda takes the Amrita but refuses to drink it. On his return he meets Vishnu, who, impressed by Garuda\u2019s restraint, grants him immortality and freedom from disease; Garuda in turn becomes Vishnu\u2019s mount. When Indra strikes him with the thunderbolt, Garuda calmly shows his invulnerability and earns Indra\u2019s respect, establishing a new cosmic alliance.\nGaruda bypasses divine defenses, slays serpent guardians, seizes the Amrita without drinking it, gains boons from Vishnu, and survives Indra\u2019s thunderbolt.\nThemes: heroic quest, self-restraint, divine trials, boons and alliances, cosmic combat", "vector": [0.01442621648311615, -0.03261340409517288, -0.010349540039896965, 0.024034542962908745, -0.012964378111064434, 0.014769370667636395, -0.027479814365506172, -0.018516618758440018, -0.021961890161037445, -0.01625179871916771, 0.02153637818992138, 0.01047307625412941, 0.023101162165403366, -0.003949708770960569, -0.004742395598441362, -0.009930891916155815, 0.05325758084654808, -0.017212631180882454, 0.030252503231167793, -0.014021294191479683, -0.008867112919688225, 0.005627734120935202, -0.014494847506284714, 0.014481120742857456, -0.005658618174493313, 0.012854568660259247, 0.006276296451687813, -0.026752326637506485, 0.00620080204680562, -0.003145011141896248, 0.0024398285895586014, 0.007103298790752888, -0.007693524472415447, 0.012779074721038342, -0.02425416186451912, -0.008894565515220165, -0.009272035211324692, -0.004244821611791849, -0.0020812321454286575, -0.007528810296207666, -0.003647732548415661, -0.